! C22-6578 PROBLEM 4.9, "COSINE OF 2 PI X", printed pp.42-43 (PDF
! 43-44), Method 2, read in the ink at 300 dpi.
!
!   The statement (printed p.42): "Given a number -1/8 <= x <= 1/8 in the
!   accumulator.  Create [cos] 2 pi x in the accumulator" -- "cos" is
!   missing in the ink (decks/problem_4_9_method1.strap).
!   "Method 2.  Since cos 2A = 2cos**2 A - 1, it is possible to reduce the
!   number of terms in the series by evaluating cos pi x first.
!   Examination shows that terms up to K = 12 would be adequate."
!
! >>> THE LAST STORE IS PRINTED "SRD(N), $L", WITH A DDS. <<<  Method 1
! prints "SRDN,$L", no dds, which both assemblers compile as the VFL STORE
! ROUNDED (C22-6578 printed p.30, "assumed VFL"; NEXT.md).  Method 2's is
! the floating-point SRD into location 8, which the model has done right
! since 2026-11-16 (decks/repro_fp_store_location8.strap).  So Method 2
! does NOT wait on the VFL SRD.  docs/source_audit.md said Method 2 had
! "the same SRDN, $L"; it does not, read at 300 dpi.
!
! THE TWENTY PRINTED CARDS FROM COSF2 TO "TEMP DR(N), (1)" ARE AS
! PRINTED but one, assembled by the host STRAP II (ASM=strap2), KONST's
! "$PI/12*$PI/11" ... arithmetic and "WON DD(N), 1.0" included (strap_asm
! refuses $PI in a DD(N): decks/repro_dd_n_math_constant.strap).
!   PRINTED ERRATUM: "E+I, (U), 1".  STRAP II refuses the card, message
!   40, EXTRA FIELDS: the dds is a field of its own after the comma.
!   Supplied "E+I(U), 1", the card the comment names ("create cos 2A":
!   EXPONENT ADD IMMEDIATE, unnormalized, plus one, doubles cos**2 A;
!   printed p.102).  Method 1's "E-I, 1" has no dds and no comma.
!   Reading: "KONST($ 2)" has a blank in the ink on the first D*N; strap2
!   assembles it to the same word as "KONST($2)" (00FC4DA2 both times).
! The deck adds START, which loads the argument and falls into COSF2,
! as for Method 1, and XARG, replaced per run by the verifier.
!
! WHAT THE PROGRAM DOES, by the Reference Manual (22-6530-2, printed
! page = PDF - 3):
!   D*(N),$L          x**2: location 8 as the operand is accumulator bits
!                     0-59 with $SB's sign (p.80), x's own 48-bit fraction.
!   SRD(N),TEMP       y = x**2 rounded (p.96).
!   the loop          five passes ($2 by CB+, XW22 count 5): acc = (WON -
!                     acc c) y, c = KONST+0..4 = pi**2/(12 11), pi**2/(10
!                     9), pi**2/(8 7), pi**2/(6 5), pi**2/(4 3); D*N is the
!                     negative multiply.
!   D*N(N),KONST($2); D+(N),WON   $2 is 5.0 after the loop: c = pi**2/2,
!                     and acc = cos pi x, the series to (pi x)**12/12!.
!   D*(N),$L          cos**2 pi x (the operand the accumulator's high 48
!                     bits); E+I(U),1 doubles it; D-(N),WON: cos 2 pi x.
!   SRD(N),$L         rounded into location 8: bits 0-59, the sign and
!                     flags to $SB bits 4-7, word 8's bits 60-63 left alone
!                     (p.80, "of both fetch and store type").
!
! THE ASSEMBLED CONSTANTS (strap2), against pi**2/(k(k-1)): every KONST
! word is truncated, 0.34, 0.90, 0.80, 0.68, 0.60, 0.95 units low; WON is
! 1 - 2**-48 ("DD(N) 1.0 IS 1 - 2^-48 UNDER STRAP II", NEXT.md).
!
! EXPECTED RESULTS ARE WORKED FROM THE PAGE, NOT THE MODEL, by
! tests/verify_problem_4_fp.py 4.9m2:<x>, sixty-digit decimal from the
! words as strap2 assembles them:
!   exact   $2 = value 5.0, count 0, refill XW22; $SB = plus, no flags
!           (cos 2 pi x > 0 on the statement's range, so this pins the
!           flags and the sign's destination, not a minus); the halt.
!   within  TEMP = round(x**2), 1 unit.
!           ACC (word 8 with $SB's sign) = the program's real number --
!           the steps above with KONST and WON as assembled and each $L
!           operand cut to 48 bits -- 4 units.
!           ACC = the page's series, K = 12, exact constants and 1, in
!           exact arithmetic: 4 units plus the distance the assembled
!           constants put between the two, worked from the deck AS IT
!           STANDS (an injected constant does not widen its own bound).
!           ACC = cos 2 pi x: that bound plus the series' own cut.
!
! MEASURED 2026-11-16, five arguments, ALL CHECKS PASSED each (2 exact
! checks and the PC, 4 within):
!   x        program-to-page  model-to-program  model-to-cos   series cut
!   1X-2        2.71 units        0.71              3.39          0.02
!   -1X-2       2.71              0.71              3.39          0.02
!   .1          2.78              0.17              2.61          0.00
!   -.1         2.78              0.17              2.61          0.00
!   .03         4.72              2.26              6.99          0.00
!   "terms up to K = 12 would be adequate" holds: the cut is .02 units at
!   the end of the range.  The few units the answer misses by are the
!   assembled constants and WON, not the series.
!
! INJECTION, DATA SIDE, OBSERVED 2026-11-16 at x = 1X-2:
!   KONST+5 "$PI/2*$PI" -> "$PI/2*3.1416" (by --sub; the as-programmed
!   number follows the injected word, the page's does not).  PREDICTED:
!   the page and cos checks only.  OBSERVED: FAIL ACC_page_series_K12 and
!   ACC_cos_2_pi_x (185157727 units each), nothing else.
!
! THE HARNESS IS NOT PRINTED: START loads XARG and falls into COSF2.
!
        SLC, 1000.0
START   DL(N), XARG
! --- printed p.43, Method 2 -------------------------------------------
COSF2   D*(N),$L
        SRD(N),TEMP
        LX, $2, XW22
DMULT   D*N(N), KONST($ 2)
        D+(N), WON
        D*(N), TEMP
        CB+, $2, DMULT
        D*N(N), KONST($2)
        D+(N), WON
        D*(N), $L                       !'create cos 2A
        E+I(U), 1                       !printed: E+I, (U), 1
        D-(N), WON
        SRD(N), $L
HALT    BEW, $
XW22    XW, 0, 5, $
KONST   DD(N), $PI/12*$PI/11,$PI/10*$PI/9
        DD(N), $PI/8*$PI/7, $PI/6*$PI/5
        DD(N),$PI/4*$PI/3,$PI/2*$PI
WON     DD(N), 1.0
TEMP    DR(N), (1)
! --- the deck's: the argument, which the verifier replaces per run ----
        SLC, 1100.0
XARG    DD(N), .1

        END, START
